<!--
    The assistant's mark: the delta, drawn to the same geometry the in-app symbol uses so
    the launcher and the running app are recognisably the same thing.

    The 108dp adaptive canvas only guarantees the middle 72dp survives every launcher mask,
    so the triangle is scaled to 54 units across rather than filling the canvas. Scaled
    from the 24-unit space of ic_delta_symbol.xml (apex 12,3 / base 3,19 to 21,19) by 3,
    which puts its bounding box at y 9..57 and x 9..63.

    Centring that box on the canvas would put the apex at y=28 and the base at y=77, and
    that is measurably low. The three sides enclose far more area near the base than near
    the apex, so the mark's mass sits at a centroid of y~60.7 against a canvas centre of
    54: centred on the box, the mark looks like it is sliding down out of the icon. Nudged
    up 4 units to y 24..73, which puts the mass back on the middle. Still comfortably
    inside the 18..90 safe zone.

    The three sides keep the weights of the in-app mark (thin on the left, heavier on
    the right) because a delta with three identical sides does not read as the same
    symbol. Monochrome launchers tint this path, so the stroke is opaque white and the
    fill transparent: an outlined mark stays legible when a themed icon flattens it to a
    single colour, which a filled one does not.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">

    <!-- Left side, thin -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="@android:color/transparent"
        android:strokeColor="#FFFFFFFF"
        android:strokeWidth="1.6"
        android:strokeLineCap="round"
        android:strokeLineJoin="round"
        android:pathData="M54,24 L27,73" />

    <!-- Base -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="@android:color/transparent"
        android:strokeColor="#FFFFFFFF"
        android:strokeWidth="1.6"
        android:strokeLineCap="round"
        android:strokeLineJoin="round"
        android:pathData="M27,73 L81,73" />

    <!-- Right side, heavier -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="@android:color/transparent"
        android:strokeColor="#FFFFFFFF"
        android:strokeWidth="3.2"
        android:strokeLineCap="butt"
        android:strokeLineJoin="round"
        android:pathData="M81,73 L54,24" />
</vector>
